		summary = '**Adventures of Huckleberry Finn** is a [[Picaresque novel|picaresque novel]] by American author [[Mark Twain]] that was first published in the United Kingdom in December 1884 and in the United States in February 1885. It is commonly named among the [[Great American Novel|Great American Novels]], and it is among the first in major [[American literature]] to be written throughout in [[Vernacular|vernacular]] English, characterized by local color regionalism. Being the direct sequel to The Adventures of Tom Sawyer, it is told in the first person by Huckleberry "Huck" Finn, the narrator of two other later Twain novels (Tom Sawyer Abroad and Tom Sawyer, Detective) and a friend of Tom Sawyer.',
